 A hand grabbed Autumn suddenly as she attempted to step off the curb and cross the street. She tried to pull away but stopped as a car speed past. 
Watch where you’re going said a deep voice from a stranger.
Oh my goodness Autumn said over the sound of her own heart pounding. You saved my life.  That truck came out of nowhere. Thank you.
The stranger stayed silent. His gaze was fixed on his own hand wrapped around her arm.
Are you ok, sir? Autumn asked. I think it safe to let go now she said with a grin.
Yes. he said finally letting go. You seem to be out of danger for now. And please call me Jack.
Autumn looked at her hero’s face for the first time and almost drowned in his dark blue eyes. She tried not to stare but between those stormy blue eyes, that five o’clock shadow and that full bottom lip…Wow.  He was the stuff wet dreams were made of.
I- um I’m Autumn she stammered 
Well I better be going. 
Of course Jack responded

Of course Jack thought. Of course she was Autumn. He was still picking his tongue up of the sidewalk. This wayward fae knock him on his ass and he could stop staring at hers as she crossed the street to the church.
He had decieded to start his search for Autumn at the orphanage. Hopeing he could catch her there. He had spotted the petite female walking down the sidewalk in his direction. In the late afternoon light he could see the feminine sway of her hips. Was almost hypnotized by it. The closer she came the more entranced he became. Now he could see the 






After the drive home Autumn couldn’t wait to shower, slip into her PJs and curl up with a good book.
When she walked through the front door she could hear the bass notes of Work by Rihanna coming from the bathroom. Which meant Vi was hitting the club tonight. Vi was a social butterfly in every way. Social because she made friends easily and  the butterfly part explained itself as Violet gave her best diva walk into the living room. 
What do you think Violet asked. Is it too naked or just naked enough?
Her wavy ombre purple hair was slicked into a high pony and matched her electric lavender heels. When a girl had features like Vi she did not hide behind hair. Not to mention the thick thighs save lives that she was serving in her well fitted black and white floral romper. Her roomate was beautiful. 
Autumn had never felt beautiful in all of her twenty six years Cute maybe but not beautiful.  Her gray eyes were a little big for her face but her lashes were nice and thick.  Her dark coils would never slick down like Vi’s. Instead Autumns hair was thick cluster of tight curls that did what the wanted. And if Autumn dared try to tame the locs with a slick back there would be hell to pay in the form of frizz.
You look great. Not too naked. Autumn said heading toward her bedroom
Thanks. Do you need help finding something to wear?
No Autumn replied. I know just the pair of comfy jammies Im looking for.
No ma’am. No jammies.  You need a night out. 
A night in? Autumn said
No you need a night out. Come dance with me Vi said winder her hips to the beat. 
Come on Autumn. It will be so much fun besides your are too young and beautiful to be in the house every weekend.
Vi you’re already dress and ready to go. I don’t want to hold you up.
Don’t even try it. It’s still early. Besides we need to eat before we leave.  Drinking on an empty stomach is not a good look.
It had been about six months since she had gone out. She would have to shake the dust off he club clothes but it would be fun to go out dancing with her bestie.
OK I’ll go. 

Two and a half hours later Autumn and Violet walked into the club. 

Purple lights swirled around the first floor. Bodies swayed to the heavy bass of the music.  The DJ was on a platform the the left that looked large enough for a live band. To the right a long padded bench lined the wall with small a small table and chair placed ever four feet or so for additional seating.  Behind the long padded bench was the stairway to the second floor. Straight ahead was the bar.  
I know where I’m headed first. Autumn said nodding toward the bar.
Shots! Shots! Shots! Good idea Violet agreed as they both started to weave there way through the sea of people on the dance floor.

Two vodka shots later Autumn felt a tingle down her back as if someone had caressed her. She turned around looking for the asshole who tried to cop a feel but no one was there.  Still she felt something.
“Autumn?” Vi called of the music. You ok?
“Yeah” Autumn said toying with her necklace. I just… It’s nothing. Its just been a while since Ive been out.
Oh ok well lets go shake the rust off. Vi grabbed my had and we headed back to the floor.
Three bass throbbing, waist winding, hip shaking songs later I still couldn’t shake the tingle down my back. 
I need a drink. Water.
Ok. I’ll come with.
No. Its ok.  Im a big girl. Besides the cutie in the hat is checking you out. Have fun.
Autumn just needed a moment to shake off the weird feeling. Plus the dance floor was packed and she had to get some air.  Autumn had no idea where she was going she just had to get away from the crowd. Absent minded she walked toward seating area but continued past the padded bench to the staircase and headed for the club’s second floor balcony. The second floor provided a birds eye view of the dance floor below.  She could see Violet slow grinding on the Spurs hat cutie.  Autumn wished she could be so care free. Even now the tingle in her spine was spreading down her legs. And she was started to feel a bit light headed. Now was not the time for a panic attack. Autumn took one step backwards away from the rail and turn to head for a seat at the bar. Instead of a clear path Autumn hit a brick wall and stumbled backward against the rails. Her heels rolled and she braced for a humiliating fall. The crash never came. In a blink she was pulled forward and pressed against the brick wall again. But this time she felt a hand against her spine and the tingle started to spread through her body. 
 His dark wavy hair fell in front of his eyes like a curtain. But beyond that wavy veil were the most seductive pair of blue eyes starring at her.  His eye seemed to glow in the club lights. At second glance that wasnt seduction in those blue eyes it was anger.
Im so sorry. Im not feeling… Nevermind I’ll just get out of your way. 
The hand on Autumn spine pressed her even more firmly against the stranger before letting go.
Please. Im the one who should watch where theyre going. I apologize for my clumsiness. Let me buy you a drink. Im River.
Im Autumn but Im just drinking water and I need to head back to my friend, Autumn said gesturing toward the dance floor below. 
The young lady with the purple hair? I saw you dancing with her. Why don’t I buy a drink for both of you and I’ll walk you back to your friend to we can have a little time to talk.
Ok. That is very nice of you.


